{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Budget and round cap are both exhausted (400/400 evals, round 4 of 4), and the run has converged on a feasible, well-covered front rather than an infeasible spec. All three constraints are demonstrably reachable: throughput best seen 171 MSPS vs >=32, max_abs_err best 1.14e-07 (2^-23.06) vs <=2.44e-04, sys_p99_batch_us best 0.257 vs <=0.5, with 218/400 evaluations feasible (183 unique) and 31 designs on the Pareto front. The front spans area_um2 41436..84011 against the HV reference 100000 and accuracy_bits 12.4..19.2 against the reference 12, i.e. it already covers both objective ranges, and this round's hypervolume gain was only +1.3% (2.852e+05), indicating diminishing returns. The selection rule (min area_um2) is satisfied by pipelined [data_width=17 n_iter=14 angle_guard=4 frac_guard=1 rounding=round] at 41436 um^2 with 12.4 accuracy bits, which clears the 2^-12 error limit with margin. unrolled_k and pipelined_m produced 0 feasible designs (max throughput 6.13 and 66.8 MSPS respectively, but no design meeting all constraints), and the unexplored iterative family is strictly slower per result than the pipelined family that dominates the front, so it cannot improve the min-area corner. No further exploration is warranted; the remaining risk is the L2 system re-selection on the shortlist, which code handles after selection."
  ,"next_plan": null
}
